Modular dungeon tiles
---------------------

Source: "Mausoleum Dungeon" by loafbrr (loafbrr.itch.io). A low-poly
crypt kit of modular walls, floors, ceilings and pillars on a 1-metre
grid, with per-material PBR textures.
License: free to use in any project, personal or commercial, with no
permission needed. Attribution is not required but is appreciated. The
full terms are in the kit's README.txt.

The maus_* pieces under content/rooms/pieces are the subset baked into
the game (a floor, a wall, a ceiling slab and a pillar, each with a
1-unit base filler), converted from the kit's combined GLB to
shared-texture meshes. It is a multi-material kit, so floors, walls, the
ceiling and the pillar each sample their own trim atlas
(content/rooms/trim_maus_*.ppm, from the kit's M_Floor_A, M_Wall_A,
M_Concrete_A and M_Trim_A diffuse maps). It clads the modular tileset
(10), which the authored DUNGEON and the generated crypt levels ride.

Modular cathedral tiles
-----------------------

Source: "Modular Cathedral Kit" by Kevin Barany / SigilsVault
(sigilsvault.itch.io). A low-poly gothic cathedral kit of walls,
floors, vaulted ceilings, columns and props on a 1-metre grid,
trim-sheet textured, with a separate stained-glass atlas.
License: CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication). Credit is appreciated but
not required. The full terms are in the kit's LICENSE.txt.

The cath_* pieces under content/rooms/pieces are the subset baked into
the game (floor, wall, vaulted ceiling, column), converted from the kit
GLBs to shared-texture meshes that sample the kit's cathedral trim
sheet. Kept at the kit's native grand scale for the cathedral theme,
and reused for the town temple from a warm-tinted bake of the same
trim sheet. cath_glass is the glass pane from the kit's window mesh,
used as an emissive clerestory wall: its diffuse is the kit's
window_diffuse, and its emission atlas (trim_cathglass_emis.ppm) is the
kit's window_emission mask tinted with stained-glass colours, so the
glass glows through the emission channel. cath_window is the kit's full
wall_window_01, a stone frame around that glass, baked as one two-material
piece: the frame samples the cathedral trim and the glass its own diffuse
and emission, so a single piece clads the framed clerestory window.

Modular cave tiles
------------------

Source: "Mines and Cave Set" by loafbrr (loafbrr.itch.io). A low-poly
organic cave and mine kit of rocky ground, cave walls, pillars, timber
and rails on a 4-metre module, with per-material PBR textures.
License: CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication). Attribution is not
required but is appreciated. The full terms are in the kit's README.txt.

The grotto_* pieces under content/rooms/pieces are the subset baked into
the game (a cave floor, a cave wall, and a ceiling reused from the floor
piece flipped to face down), converted from the kit's combined GLB to
shared-texture meshes. Floors and the ceiling sample the ground atlas
and the walls sample the cave-rock atlas (content/rooms/trim_grotto_*.ppm,
from the kit's Mines_Ground and Mine_Walls diffuse maps). It clads the
crystal grotto on tileset 13. The 1-unit base fillers are flat quads,
not kit meshes.

Volcanic rock tiles
-------------------

Source: "Canyon Terrain" by loafbrr (loafbrr.itch.io). A low-poly canyon
kit of warm rusty rock ground and wall tiles, rock formations and desert
plants on a 4-metre module, with per-material textures.
License: CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication). Attribution is not required
but is appreciated. The full terms are in the kit's README.txt.

The volc_* pieces under content/rooms/pieces are the ground and wall
tiles (plus flat 1-unit fillers), converted to shared-texture meshes that
sample the kit's CanyonGround and CanyonWall_3 diffuse maps
(content/rooms/trim_volc_*.ppm). The warm basalt clads the INFERNAL
volcanic cavern on tileset 15, and a lava-lake sector on tileset 16 adds
a lava emission atlas (content/rooms/trim_lava_emis.ppm) so the floor
glows molten. The lava emission is a procedural placeholder (a fire
colour ramp over fractal noise, made with ImageMagick, not from any kit),
marked for replacement with authored lava art.

Door prop
---------

Source: "Low Poly Doors" by loafbrr (loafbrr.itch.io). A low-poly set of
framed doors with a shared colour-variant texture atlas.
License: CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication). Attribution is not required
but is appreciated. The full terms are in the kit's README.txt.

content/models/doorway.obj is the first door group (the panel, frame and
outer frame), converted from the kit's GLTF to an embedded-texture prop
mesh. Its texture (content/models/doorway.ppm) is the brown colour
variant, cropped to the door's region of the atlas and the mesh UVs
remapped to it so the small prop texture carries full detail. It replaces
the earlier image-generated doorway prop and the flat exit-door billboard,
and the renderer stands it in every door portal.

Ladder prop
-----------

Source: "Ladder" by trillobit3s (trillobit3s-indie-games.itch.io). A
low-poly wooden ladder model with a single diffuse texture.
License: freeware, free to use in your projects, with an optional
donation to support the author. Attribution is not required. The terms
are on the asset's itch.io page.
  https://trillobit3s-indie-games.itch.io/ladder

content/models/ladder.obj is the model converted from the kit's FBX to an
embedded-texture prop mesh, and content/models/ladder.ppm is its diffuse
texture cropped to the mesh's UV region and the UVs remapped to it so the
