Spell catalog
-------------

Source: the AX&X spell lists (the author's own two-page OSR ruleset, a refit
of the classic 1st Edition advanced rules). content/spells.txt is imported
from that project's spells.csv: the Cleric, Druid, and Magic-User lists across
six spell levels, with each spell's terse effect prose kept as the behaviour.
The spell names follow the long-standing lineage AX&X refits.

The crawler reads the prose as the real behaviour and maps each spell's damage
type onto its own five elements thematically, so combat that wires a spell up
approximates the intent rather than reproducing exact tabletop mechanics.

Animated character sheets (GandalfHardcore)
-------------------------------------------

Source: character and NPC pixel-art packs by GandalfHardcore
(gandalfhardcore.itch.io), purchased and licensed by the author for personal
and commercial use.
License: the pack terms permit use in free and commercial games and projects
and editing the art. They do NOT permit redistributing or reselling the images
on their own or as part of an asset-pack compilation, nor use for AI training.
This is not a CC0 asset: the terms above govern it, not the CC0 note at the top
of this file.

content/banks/sheets holds the sheet PNGs and their sliced banks. Each sheet is
a grid of 64x64 cells, a column per character and a row per animation frame; the
offline sheet slicer (tools/mkassets `sheet` verb) carves each column into a
bank lump. The character grids give one bank per column (a 13-frame idle cycle);
the enemy sheets give one bank per creature, sliced by action row (idle, walk,
attack, death), each row a sequence with its own frame count. Imported so far:

  male.sheet    MALE_GUARD, MALE_PEASANT, MALE_CULTIST, MALE_MERCENARY,
                MALE_BISHOP, MALE_SOLDIER, MALE_DWARF, MALE_KING, MALE_HUNTER,
                MALE_BARREL, MALE_KNIGHT
  female.sheet  FEMALE_QUEEN, FEMALE_DRYAD, FEMALE_NUN, FEMALE_BARLADY,
                FEMALE_MAID, FEMALE_KNIGHT, FEMALE_VAMPIRE, FEMALE_MERCHANT,
                FEMALE_SUCCUBUS
  enemy pack    ORC, RAT, LAMIA, BARELAMIA, MIMIC, MUSHROOM, PLANT (idle, walk,
                attack, death); BAT (idle, walk, death); FLYINGWITCH, PUMPKIN
                (idle, attack, death); MOSQUITO, FLYINGEYE (idle, walk). One
                .sheet manifest per creature PNG (orc.sheet, rat.sheet, ...).
  archer        ARCHER and seven recolors (ARCHER_BLACK, _BLUE, _BROWN, _GREEN,
                _PURPLE, _RED, _YELLOW), each idle, walk, shoot, hurt, death.
  zombie        ZOMBIE and ZOMBIE_V2/_V3/_V4 (four designs), idle, walk, attack,
                hurt, death read from a wrapping strip (the crawl is left out).
  skeleton      SKELETON and recolors (_WHITE, _GHOST, _GOLD, _RED, _RETRO),
                idle, walk, attack, death from a wrapping strip.
  goblin        GOBLIN and recolors (_BRIGHT, _BROWN, _DARK, _LIME, _RED),
                72x80 cells, idle, walk, attack, hurt, death from a strip.
  spider        SPIDER, 96x96 cells, idle, walk, attack, death (16-wide sheet).
  samurai       SAMURAI and seven recolors (_BLACK, _BLUE, _GREEN, _PURPLE,
                _RED, _WHITE, _YELLOW), 96x64 cells, idle, walk, attack, hurt,
                death; the many extra slash and spin rows are left unimported.
  angel         ANGEL, 96x96 cells, idle, flight (as walk), a light cast.
  wizard        WIZARD and seven recolors (_BLACK, _BROWN, _GREEN, _PURPLE,
                _RED, _WHITE, _YELLOW), idle, walk, cast, hurt, death; the many
                extra spell rows are left unimported.
  alien         ALIEN gunner, idle, walk, shoot, death (run-and-gun rows out).
  knight        KNIGHT and recolors (_BLACK, _BROWN, _GREEN), 69x58 cells,
                idle, walk, attack, block, death.
  horse         HORSE (+_BLACK, _WHITE), 128x90, idle, walk, run, death.
  farm animals  COW (+_BW, _RED) 112x80, PIG (+_BLACK, _BROWN) 80x48 idle/walk/
                graze; CHICKEN (+_BLACK, _WHITE) 32x32 idle/walk/peck.
  mounted knight RIDER and seven recolors, 128x111, idle, walk, lance charge,
                gallop, death.
  agent soldier AGENT (+_GREEN), 64x64, idle, walk, shoot, death; the many
                aim-angle and prone rows are left unimported.
  heavy knight  HKNIGHT and seven recolors, 91x64, idle, walk, attack, block,
                death (the pack's extra sheet2 and run strips are not imported).
  maid          MAID and seven recolors, 64x64, idle, walk, death; the serving
                and curtsy rows, and the pack's "full" outfit variants and the
                combat/witch-hat sheets, are not imported yet.
  medieval woman MAIDEN, 64x64, idle, walk, harp, death.
  female agent  FAGENT and four recolors, 64x64, idle, walk, shoot, death; the
                aim-angle and prone rows are not imported.

Single-character packs ship several recolors and lay their actions out as one
strip that wraps across rows, so those banks are sliced with the `lin` run (a
row-major cell range) and one bank is baked per recolor.

Because the pack terms forbid redistributing the art on its own, keep the sheet
PNGs out of any public mirror of this repository, or replace them there with the
baked pak, which embeds only the game's own use of the frames.

Bundled libraries (macOS)
-------------------------

Source: Simple DirectMedia Layer 2 (SDL2) by Sam Lantinga and the SDL
contributors, https://www.libsdl.org/.
License: zlib license (free to use and redistribute, including commercially;
an acknowledgement is appreciated but not required).

On the other targets the game loads the system or distribution SDL2 at
runtime. The macOS .app has no system SDL2 to find, so it bundles the
official SDL2 framework binary (version 2.32.10, a universal arm64 and
x86_64 Mach-O) in Contents/Frameworks and loads it from there. The dylib
is supplied at build time and is not stored in this repository; see
docker/macos-cross/README.md for how it is obtained.
